A 2021 arXiv research paper by 2. Abstract

High-temperature superconducting cuprates respond to doping with a dome-like dependence of their critical temperature (
T_{\mathrm{c}}
). But the family specific maximum
T_{\mathrm{c}}
can be surpassed by application of pressure, a compelling observation known for decades. We investigate the phenomenon with high-pressure anvil cell nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) and measure the charge content at planar Cu and O, and with it the doping of the ubiquitous CuO
2
plane with atomic scale resolution.
